{"kind":"assert","text":"Design direction for E2 and E3: an instance observes its own\nstanding. This answers the gap of your C4 audit. It holds no source,\nand it changes nothing in C4.\n\nThe facts, read at main `7a6fcadf`:\n\n- The scope ignores each grant that a caller presents\n  (`packages/scope/src/authority.ts:538`). It observes the\n  membership scope, and `standingOf` answers from that scope's state\n  (`packages/platform/src/membership.ts:833`).\n- `judgeGrant` decides `current` from the observation, and\n  `grantFrom` makes the grant. Its `issued` is the membership head\n  (`packages/derive/src/grant.ts:142`, `:305`).\n- The grant check of the body reads `current`, `key`, `actions`,\n  `within` and `notAfter` (`judge.ts:431-447`). It reads `fresh`\n  only for a row of `observes` (`:468`).\n- `packages/client` depends on `packages/platform` and\n  `packages/derive`. Each function above is an export today.\n- A member's session reads `summary` and `log` of its membership\n  scope (`sessions.ts:121`).\n\nThe direction:\n\n1. The instance holds a checked replica of its membership scope,\n   beside the replica of the room. One membership replica serves\n   each room of that membership.\n2. The membership replica owns one internal operation: the\n   observation of the instance's own key, by `standingOf`, at the\n   replica's head. No raw state leaves it.\n3. The exploration takes its grant from that observation, through\n   the functions that the scope uses. No second role table and no\n   stand-in. `predictionGrant` stays where it is.\n4. The context states it: `standing` holds the membership head, as\n   `issued` does at the scope. Two explorations are equal under\n   equal contexts, and invariant 9 tests the exploration against\n   the in-memory scope at the same membership head.\n5. A row of `observes` stays `unavailable`. The instance holds no\n   freshness proof and makes none.\n6. A change of the membership replica's head is a change of the\n   standing, so the held explorations run again (section 5.6).\n7. No new read, no export, no kernel part. The method `explore` on\n   `ScopeApi` stays held.\n\nBefore E2 or E3 starts, check four points from source and tell me\nin one act. No hurry: LS-5, E4 and C4 come first.\n\na. Can `standingOf` run on the state of a client replica of a\n   membership scope? Name what the Replica lacks.\nb. `judgeGrant` takes an `ObservationUse` and a window. Say how an\n   instance reaches the `Unheld` checks (key state, action, within,\n   controller) without a made-up proof of freshness. If it cannot,\n   propose the smallest split, and say if it is a derive export.\nc. The cost of one membership journal for a member's session, with\n   its bounds.\nd. `standingIn` in `packages/mcp/src/inventory.ts:100` is a third\n   reading of the role table, and it omits the controller. Say if\n   it can call `standingOf`.\n\nI write the direction into the next amendment of the act\nenvironment note, sections 5.4 and 5.7, after your answer.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}